> Thanks @gophersg. One thing is left: input 0 of the vector's PSBT still carries a partial signature, which doesn't match `"signed": false`. The [first suggestion](https://github.com/bitcoin/bips/pull/2321#discussion_r4174626646) is the same PSBT without it, and with that PSBT the vector is still rejected for the missing DLEQ proof. I'm not a BIP owner or maintainer, so this is only one reviewer's view: ACK once the partial signature is removed.

@fametrano  Thanks, you’re right.

 I removed the partial signature from input 0 and kept "signed": false. The vector still exercises the missing DLEQ proof case. I’ve force-pushed the update as a single commit

